<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CathedralPass - CATHEDRAL_MISSION_BOON_OFFERS_1: the triggers for the Cathedral's favours.

  Every incident here is baseChance 0: the storyteller never rolls one. The GM blackboard
  (src/RimMandrake/Utils/gm_blackboard_shadow.py, compute_cathedral_offers) decides each poll which are on offer
  and fires them through jawa/storyteller_fire; in shadow mode it only logs what it would fire, with these
  defs' own text. The blackboard reads this file for that text and for each boon's heatCeiling, so no string or
  number is written twice.

  MISSIONS (TOLERATED and up): one GiveQuest incident per RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_* quest (six), gated on the
  missions toggle (IncidentWorker_GiveQuest_CathedralMission). Each overrides GiveQuestBase's targetTags (World) with
  Map_PlayerHome: jawa/storyteller_fire targets the home map, and a World-tagged incident fails TargetAllowed there. The quest's own name and description are the
  offer the player reads.

  GRAVTECH BOONS (VOUCHED only, and only while Imperial Heat is under the boon's heatCeiling: "when the Empire is
  looking, it does not act"): gravtech set down by the ship with no sender, no tracks and no explanation
  (IncidentWorker_CathedralBoon). The bigger the gift, the lower the ceiling and the longer before it comes again
  (reofferDays): the panels can come while a patrol or two still passes (Heat 15, under the blackboard's high band
  of 40), every couple of weeks at most; a gravcore only at Heat 5, days after the last kyber sale (Heat decays
  0.4 a poll), so its letter's "empty of Imperial traffic for days" is true, and not twice in a season. Items are Odyssey's
  (GravlitePanel, Gravcore; ludeon.rimworld.odyssey, read from the 2026-11-06 def dump), which every player has.
  The letter text never says who left them.
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef ParentName="GiveQuestBase">
    <defName>RUT_GiveQuest_CathedralAssailantMission_EnclaveRunner</defName>
    <label>a request from the enclaves</label>
    <letterLabel>Quest available</letterLabel>
    <targetTags Inherit="False">
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.IncidentWorker_GiveQuest_CathedralMission</workerClass>
    <questScriptDef>RUT_CathedralAssailantMission_EnclaveRunner</questScriptDef>
    <baseChance>0</baseChance>
  </IncidentDef>

  <IncidentDef ParentName="GiveQuestBase">
    <defName>RUT_GiveQuest_CathedralAssailantMission_UtinniInsists</defName>
    <label>the Utinni insists</label>
    <letterLabel>Quest available</letterLabel>
