  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_CathedralGravtechBoon_GravlitePanels</defName>
    <label>panels on the ramp</label>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.IncidentWorker_CathedralBoon</workerClass>
    <baseChance>0</baseChance>
    <letterLabel>Panels on the ramp</letterLabel>
    <letterText>At first light the deck crew found a stack of gravlite panels on the cargo ramp, squared off neatly and still cold from the night. No tracks led to them and none led away.\n\nNobody aboard claims them, and nobody wants to ask too loudly. There was no patrol overhead last night.</letterText>
    <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.RUT_CathedralBoonExtension">
        <gifts>
          <GravlitePanel>30</GravlitePanel>
        </gifts>
        <heatCeiling>15</heatCeiling>
        <reofferDays>15</reofferDays>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </IncidentDef>

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_CathedralGravtechBoon_Gravcore</defName>
    <label>a gravcore in the sand</label>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.IncidentWorker_CathedralBoon</workerClass>
    <baseChance>0</baseChance>
    <letterLabel>A gravcore in the sand</letterLabel>
    <letterText>The perimeter lights caught it an hour before dawn: a gravcore, whole and faintly warm, set upright in the sand just outside the ship's shadow. It is older than anything in your stores, and it fits the Utinni's sockets as if it had been cut for them.\n\nThe sky has been empty of Imperial traffic for days.</letterText>
    <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.CathedralPass.RUT_CathedralBoonExtension">
        <gifts>
          <Gravcore>1</Gravcore>
        </gifts>
        <heatCeiling>5</heatCeiling>
        <reofferDays>45</reofferDays>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
